From: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mali_kbase: port hrtimer_init()+.function to hrtimer_setup()

Kernel 7.2 removed hrtimer_init(timer, clock_id, mode) (the two-step
"hrtimer_init() then separately assign timer->function") in favour of
a single hrtimer_setup(timer, function, clock_id, mode) call.

Mechanically port all 11 call sites across 6 files to the combined
API. Every site already assigned ->function immediately after
hrtimer_init() and before any hrtimer_start(), so this is a faithful
1:1 semantic replacement.

Fixes the mali_kbase.ko build against kernel 7.2.0-rc4-sky1-ncz.
Codex (gpt-5.5) adversarial-reviewed: APPROVE.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_kinstr_prfcnt.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_kinstr_prfcnt.c
@@ -1269,8 +1269,8 @@
 
 	mutex_init(&kinstr_ctx->lock);
 	INIT_LIST_HEAD(&kinstr_ctx->clients);
-	hrtimer_init(&kinstr_ctx->dump_timer, CLOCK_MONOTONIC, HRTIMER_MODE_REL);
-	kinstr_ctx->dump_timer.function = kbasep_kinstr_prfcnt_dump_timer;
+	hrtimer_setup(&kinstr_ctx->dump_timer, kbasep_kinstr_prfcnt_dump_timer, CLOCK_MONOTONIC,
+		      HRTIMER_MODE_REL);
 	INIT_WORK(&kinstr_ctx->dump_work, kbasep_kinstr_prfcnt_dump_worker);
 
 	*out_kinstr_ctx = kinstr_ctx;
